2026-09-24T21:33:35.4456917Z ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-09-24T21:33:35.4457608Z   PASS  timing 0 < w <= s < t <= 3  -- (w, s, t) = (2, 2, 3)
2026-09-24T21:33:35.4458415Z   PASS  W, write  -- a seed of positive prior whose hidden state at w separates the roots
2026-09-24T21:33:35.4459300Z   PASS  S, overlap  -- Gamma_2(a, x) = 1/4, Gamma_2(b, x) = 1/4
2026-09-24T21:33:35.4460051Z   PASS  S, store  -- the root-conditioned seed weights at x differ
2026-09-24T21:33:35.4461235Z   PASS  R(1), causal read  -- the two weights, propagated from (x, -), give different visible laws at t
2026-09-24T21:33:35.4462233Z   PASS  R(2), rooted reappearance  -- the rooted rows at t = 3 differ
2026-09-24T21:33:35.4463246Z   PASS  RD6-a: LatticeCutReadback 1 4 2 1 {0} uniform 3  -- witness a = (0, 0), b = (1, 0), (w, s, t) = (2, 2, 3), x = (1, 0)
2026-09-24T21:33:35.4464121Z 
2026-09-24T21:33:35.4464358Z RD6-a and RD6-b -- exhaustive search at both windows
2026-09-24T21:33:35.4465020Z ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-09-24T21:33:35.4465825Z   PASS  the frozen witness is among the window-3 witnesses  -- 48 witnesses at K = 3
2026-09-24T21:33:35.4466867Z   PASS  RD6-b: no witness at window 2  -- every root pair, every admissible (w, s, t) and every visible value checked
2026-09-24T21:33:35.4467572Z 
2026-09-24T21:33:35.4467720Z what this does NOT show
2026-09-24T21:33:35.4468205Z ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2026-09-24T21:33:35.4469029Z   The lattice predicate is not vacuous on the manuscripts' own dynamics: it fires at
2026-09-24T21:33:35.4469963Z   window 3 and not at window 2 on a four-site torus with a one-site region. That is
2026-09-24T21:33:35.4470862Z   the entire content. This is NOT [SM] Theorem 22's readback genericity lemma -- the
2026-09-24T21:33:35.4471829Z   lemma quantifies over connected regions with |V| <= N/3, and the instance fixes one
2026-09-24T21:33:35.4472825Z   region, one size and one alphabet. It is not a physical statement: L = 4 is no
2026-09-24T21:33:35.4473977Z   lattice cut of our universe, and no accessibility clock is attached to it. It moves
2026-09-24T21:33:35.4474918Z   the P1 row's status by nothing, and it says nothing about the cosmological cut.
2026-09-24T21:33:35.4475818Z   Forbidden in terms: 'C4 holds at the lattice cut', 'the lattice cut is discharged',
2026-09-24T21:33:35.4476594Z   'the genericity lemma holds in an instance'.
